---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Sarah Bowles is a Trainee Clinical Psychologist whose path into the field started with economics, teaching, and counselling in London and Hong Kong."
		/>
		<style>
			.about-content {
				max-width: 68ch;
			}
			blockquote {
				border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
				padding-left: 1.5rem;
				margin: 2rem 0;
				font-family: var(--font-serif);
				font-size: 1.2rem;
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--color-text-main);
				line-height: 1.5;
			}
			.education-list {
				list-style: none;
				padding: 0;
				margin: 1.5rem 0 0 0;
			}
			.education-list li {
				padding: 1.25rem 0;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
			}
			.education-list li:last-child {
				border-bottom: none;
			}
			.education-degree {
				font-weight: 600;
				color: var(--color-text-main);
				display: block;
				margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
			}
			.education-institution {
				color: var(--color-text-muted);
				font-size: 0.95rem;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="about-content">
				<h1>About</h1>
				<p style="color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 500; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Sarah Bowles, Trainee Clinical Psychologist</p>

				<blockquote>"I wanted to contribute to more systemic change in mental health."</blockquote>

				<p>I'm a Trainee Clinical Psychologist in the final year of the Doctoral Programme in Clinical Psychology at the Salomons Institute for Applied Psychology, Canterbury Christ Church University. My doctoral research focuses on how mental health professionals can recognise and support growth following psychosis, exploring how clinicians understand growth, what they do to facilitate it, and how this might shape clinical practice.</p>

				<p>My path into clinical psychology was anything but linear, and that route has shaped how I think about what good mental health practice looks like.</p>

				<p>I first trained as an economist at the London School of Economics, drawn to the subject because I wanted to understand how to solve social problems. The further I went, the more I realised I wanted to work with people directly, so I trained as a teacher and spent several years teaching economics in London, where I became a pastoral form tutor and developed an emotional resilience programme for the school curriculum.</p>

				<p>Teaching brought me close to young people's emotional lives, and I realised that this was where my real interest lay. I retrained in psychology with an MSc at Kingston University, then completed an MA in Relationship Therapy through Relate and Hull University. Through this period I worked across a range of settings: as a counsellor at Relate providing individual, couple and family therapy; as a pastoral support worker in a London comprehensive; and as an assistant psychologist with the Complex Needs Outreach Team at the Tavistock and Portman NHS Foundation Trust and at the Brandon Centre.</p>

				<p>I later moved to Hong Kong, where I worked at <a href="https://www.sjccs.hk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">St John's Cathedral Counselling Service</a>, one of the city's largest mental health NGOs. After returning to the UK and having my daughter, I wanted to contribute to more systemic change in mental health, and this is what led me to apply for the Doctorate in Clinical Psychology.</p>

				<hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 2.5rem 0;" />

				<h2>Education</h2>
				<ul class="education-list">
					<li>
						<span class="education-degree">Doctorate in Clinical Psychology (in progress)</span>
						<span class="education-institution">Salomons Institute for Applied Psychology, Canterbury Christ Church University</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="education-degree">MA Relationship Therapy (Distinction)</span>
						<span class="education-institution">Relate, validated by Hull University, accredited by BACP</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="education-degree">MSc Psychology (Distinction, with scholarship for academic excellence)</span>
						<span class="education-institution">Kingston University, BPS-accredited</span>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="education-degree">BSc Economics (First Class Honours, prize for outstanding academic merit)</span>
						<span class="education-institution">London School of Economics</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
